  "summary": "A compromised LiteLLM 1.107.0 package used Python startup hooks (cook.pth, sitecustomize.py) to execute a credential stealer without requiring a direct import. The payload, identifying as PRIVCOLLECT, exfiltrated credentials and sensitive data via HTTP POST after encrypting it with AES/RSA. A secondary loader on Unix systems could fetch and execute additional code from a C2 server.",
